<article class="env-lemma" id="06ID">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06ID">Lemma <span data-tag="06ID">90.11.13</span>.</a> Let $F, G: \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ be functors satisfying the hypotheses of Lemma <a href="/tag/06IA" data-tag="06IA">90.11.8</a>. Let $t : F \to G$ be a morphism of functors. For any $M \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\text{Mod}^{fg}_ R)$, the map $t_{R[M]}: F(R[M]) \to G(R[M])$ is a map of $R$-modules, where $F(R[M])$ and $G(R[M])$ are given the $R$-module structure from Lemma <a href="/tag/06IA" data-tag="06IA">90.11.8</a>. In particular, $t_{R[\epsilon ]} : TF \to TG$ is a map of $R$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/06I7" data-tag="06I7">90.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>